Q: Is there a way to set &quot;Session ID&quot; when using Azure.Monitor.OpenTelemetry.AspNetCore A: <p>You can find a great deal of information about this in the following locations:</p>
<ol>
<li><a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/blob/next/semantic-conventions/src/experimental_attributes.ts#L2558" rel="nofollow noreferrer">OpenTelemetry's JavaScript SDK's Source</a> which seems to suggest <code>enduser.id</code> is deprecated</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-net/issues/45089" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Support setting User ID and Session ID via Azure Monitor's Otel Exporter</a></li>
<li>The natural lead on from this of: <a href="https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-net/issues/46021" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Support Setting/Overriding any attribute via the Otel Exporter</a></li>
</ol>
<p>The last post on some of the related issues, questions the priority of these items but I wasn't able to find much else.</p>
<p>UPDATE: I have done some additional research and, for tags on your activities you can use:</p>
<ol>
<li>Setting <code>enduser.id</code> populates <code>user_AutheticatedId</code> - <a href="https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-net/pull/36509" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-net/pull/36509</a></li>
<li>Setting <code>enduser.pseudo.id</code> populates <code>user_userId</code> - Found in another pr - <a href="https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-net/pull/52722" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-net/pull/52722</a></li>
<li>Setting <code>microsoft.session.id</code> populates <code>session_id</code>. - Couldn't find the PR but lucky guess.</li>
</ol>
<p>For my testing I used:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>public static class ActivityExtensions
{
    public static void ApplyPseudonymousId(this Activity activity, PseudonymousId id)
    {
        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(activity, nameof(activity));

        activity.SetTag(MetricsHelper.UserIDTag, id);
        activity.AddBaggage(MetricsHelper.UserIDTag, id);

        // SET ALL THE THINGS (for testing)
        activity.SetTag(&quot;enduser.id&quot;, id);
        activity.AddBaggage(&quot;enduser.id&quot;, id);

        activity.SetTag(&quot;user.id&quot;, id);
        activity.AddBaggage(&quot;user.id&quot;, id);

        activity.SetTag(&quot;microsoft.session.id&quot;, id);
        activity.AddBaggage(&quot;microsoft.session.id&quot;, id);

        activity.SetTag(&quot;enduser.pseudo.id&quot;, id);
        activity.AddBaggage(&quot;enduser.pseudo.id&quot;, id);

    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>And a very simple middleware:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>public class UserIDTagMiddleware
{
    private readonly RequestDelegate Next;

    private readonly IUserAnonymizer Anonymizer;

    public UserIDTagMiddleware(RequestDelegate next, IUserAnonymizer anonymizer)
    {
        Next = next;
        Anonymizer = anonymizer;
    }

    public async Task InvokeAsync(HttpContext context)
    {
        // For tracing, logging and metrics, we store the userid on the Activity.
        // https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/app/opentelemetry-add-modify?tabs=aspnetcore#set-the-user-id-or-authenticated-user-id
        var userId = context.User.FindFirst(ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier)?.Value;
        if (userId != null)
        {
            var psuedo = PseudonymousId.From(Anonymizer, userId);
            Activity.Current?.ApplyPseudonymousId(psuedo);
        }

        await Next(context);
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>These were just test values at the time, so I was please to see, the following in the requests table:
<a href="https://i.sstatic.net/J91LMm2C.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/J91LMm2C.png" alt="All suitable userID fields and session id filled in, within application insights" /></a></p>
<p>I am currently unable to get them into traces or customEvents though, so I will keep poking.</p>
